      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are correct that the preponderance of modern urban planning research identifies restrictive single-family zoning as a primary driver of the housing crisis, as it artificially constrain supply, drives up prices, and increases per-unit environmental impact. While some historical arguments for preserving neighborhood character exist, they generally fail to hold up against empirical evidence showing that affordable housing solutions require more regulation and densification. The consensus among major organizations like the National Association of Home Builders and the American Planning Association now heavily favors removing single-family restrictions to achieve both economic recovery and sustainable community outcomes.",
